<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cantigas de Santa Maria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">13th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Cantigas de Santa María</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Cantigas de Santa Maria are a collection of over 400 songs in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galician-portuguese">Galician-Portuguese</a> in praise of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mary-mother-of-jesus">Virgin Mary</a>, compiled at the court of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-x-of-castile">Alfonso X of Castile</a> in the later 13th century. Most tell of miracles of the Virgin, and the illuminated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuscript">manuscripts</a>, with musical notation and hundreds of miniatures, are among the great works of medieval music and art.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cantigas-de-santa-maria.jpg" alt="Cantigas de Santa Maria" width="320" height="667" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The court of Alfonso X (1251-1284) From the Patrimonio Nacional website:&quot; we can affirm that it is a collective creat... · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Anafil_players,_Cantigas_de_Santa_Maria,_Bl-2_286R_cropped_with_music.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
